{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"harmless-unfair-borer","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observed problem\n`infra/gerrit/feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh::scenario_4` reads the post-remerge Verified vote into `ver_after` and emits `EVIDENCE: ... expect=LLM_carried_VER_rerun`, but its only assertions after the push check `MERGE_FIRST_PARENT_UPDATE` and LLM-Review carry. The final `pass` line still says `Verified re-runs (${ver_after})` for any recorded value. A run can therefore report scenario 4 passed while Verified rerun was never proved.\n\n## Scope\nCorrect the executable success/reporting behavior in scenario 4. Decide whether the scenario should assert a rerun or report the observed vote without claiming one. Keep the existing LLM carry assertion, `EVIDENCE:` schema, and sourced-driver API. This is outside the comment-only remediation leaf `chargeful-untimely-midge`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Scenario 4 cannot emit a passing statement that asserts Verified reran unless an executable check proves that rerun.\n- [ ] The new check or narrower message is covered by a focused test of the scenario output/exit behavior.\n- [ ] Existing `EVIDENCE:` fields and LLM-Review carry assertion remain intact.\n- [ ] Shell validation, focused Gerrit tests, and repository verification pass.","id":"3781-9cec-5cf5-46be","parent_id":"","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Scenario 4 claims Verified reran without asserting it"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792758158900363239,"uuid":"9f20f94a-0c8a-457a-bdc4-880d28f6b4e1"}